# Fensterladen: a guest-house shutter hinged above its window (timed
# one-way platform, D-094; k outline on the shutter). open: folded out flat
# as a ledge, k top edge on row 0 over all 32 px with the o lip on row 1
# (the walking line, the Gondel/Traundl convention), G slats with j gaps,
# a j front edge and k underside (rows 0-6), d iron stays down to the wall
# beside the window. The window i/m frame, a dark d room with w/i lace
# curtains, a wooden O/l geranium box (dark top edge, no lip) with g/G
# leaves and p/E flowers. rattle: the landlady's arm e/E with a dirndl
# sleeve R/r reaches up to the ledge; frame 1 shifts the shutter, its stays
# and the arm 1 px down (renderer shake; the body never moves). closed: the
# shutter hangs inside the window frame (k outline, G/j louvres, lit g
# stile), from a d hinge rail whose knuckles break its top, with the i
# frame still showing around it: a shut window, nothing that reads as a
# surface. warn: the shutter lifts out from the bottom (shorter)
# and the landlady peeks out, w/i headscarf, e/E face, k eyes looking left
# then right. Faces the viewer, no mirror. Generated by the pixel-artist
# with a throwaway script; the grids are the source.
sprite = fensterladen
size   = 32x24
origin = 16,24
hitbox = 0,0,32,8
anim   = open frames=1
anim   = rattle frames=2 ticks=4 loop
anim   = closed frames=1
anim   = warn frames=2 ticks=8 loop
